From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 13:32:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] bundler: support module-scoped Node pools

Recognize paired "use node" and "use node pool:<name>" directives on root function entries. Validate pool names, reserve the default executor name, attach the required pool-bearing environment and explicit pool field only to the corresponding entry output, and leave shared chunks in the ordinary Node environment.

Require pool metadata to agree with the module environment in both full-module and hash-only deployment schemas. Include the metadata in changed-module comparison and deployment records so a pool move cannot be reported as unchanged, while preserving component rejection of Node modules.

Add focused coverage for directive parsing, entry-output association, dependency chunks, reserved names, schema agreement, and unchanged-module metadata.
